        "thought_text": "Revised Thought-1: Instead of using dynamic programming to track safe paths, consider a greedy approach where we try to move the torpedo diagonally up-left, up-right, or straight up at each step, avoiding any ships. If at any point the torpedo cannot move without hitting a ship, mark that direction as blocked and try the next available direction. If all directions are blocked, backtrack and explore alternative paths. This approach ensures that we find a valid path if one exists, or determine that it's impossible otherwise.",
